{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1534713-need-advice-on-running-very-secure-pentex-site","id":1534713,"title":"Need advice on running very secure Pentex site","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-25T12:29:14-07:00","id":1534713,"title":"Need advice on running very secure Pentex site","content":"Hey everyone, this weekend I've offered to run a werewolf game with very little prep and suddenly find myself scrambling. I am going to be running a classic raid on a secure Pentax location, and while I'm flipping source books and trying to come up with the obstacles and defenses the players will run into, I was hoping for some expert advice from you guys. <br /> <br /> The site is Sudbury, Ontario, where the SNOLAB science lab is located two kilometers underground. It's surrounded by highly toxic and polluted mining activity, and is perfect for a long weekend raid.<br /> <br /> The players are playing three Adren, and Will be part of a much larger attack force. <br /> <br /> So my question is: what sort of defenses and wyrm or weaver spirits would you expect them to run into in such a secure facility? I could imagine your basic high level human and fomori security teams, all sorts of mundane security measures, perhaps a local black spiral dancer pack, toxic banes, maybe even some weaver myrmidon units, but what else you think would be fun and exciting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T14:46:48-07:00","id":1534736,"title":"","content":"First it might be worth asking &quot;what have they got here that's worth guarding?&quot; If you answer that, you'll probably be on the way toward selecting whatever First Teams, fomori, BSDs, fallen Fera, weird banes, and crossover madness that it might be employing to keep the site secure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T18:54:41-07:00","id":1534745,"title":"","content":"Try to create challenges that rewards the Gifts the players have taken for their characters. You want to encourage solutions to challenges that are more than just &quot;I hit it very hard.&quot; But you just can't create a challenge that the players do not have the right Gift for. So you need to customize it. Hopefully they'll give you their character sheet ahead of time. For example, if one or more PCs have Resist Toxin, then it'd be good to use poison gas in one or more encounters so they can shine. If someone has Call of Rust, make sure there is some barrier made of iron that would otherwise be hard to remove.<br /> <br /> For challenges in the Penumbra, have both intentional defenses (that PENTEX set up and controls)) and unintentional hazards (that simply exist because of the local environment and PENTEX does not control it).<br /> <br /> You may want to have a specific area/room of the facility be warded against Garou so they cannot enter it without rolling Willpower or spending Willpower.<br /> <br /> Panic rooms, fail safes, and booby traps are all good to complicate things after the PCs have a success. Maybe if they break into certain areas, a Wyrm Tunnel (equivalent to a Moon Bridge) appears and begins to transport Banes into the area). Having the stereotypical death trap like in the Resident Evil movie is good as long as you can make it exciting and more than just a make one roll or die situation. You want something that rewards creativity by the players to get around it.<br /> <br /> If they begin to ask questions like 'Is there an air duct, or is there a water pipe nearby&quot; then say &quot;yes&quot; most of the time. It shows they are being creative. Just be ready to improvise.<br /> <br /> And remember even ordinary people can be a hazard if they have a pistol that has silver bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 04-26-2024, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T19:12:44-07:00","id":1534789,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if one thing is certain, it is silver. PENTEX always has plenty and that's the only real constant here.<br /> <br /> Other than everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said, I'd just add pure weirdness. Be it lovecraftian weirdness created by the toxic environment, or comedic weirdness created by PENTEX's ludicrously toxic office environment.\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}